14.2 Multi‑Attribute Trade Study

A weighted‑sum utility function is employed:

U = \sum_{i=1}^{5} v_i \, u_i(\text{mass, endurance, protection factor, cost, comfort}),

with weights v_i elicited from stakeholder panels via the Analytic Hierarchy Process (AHP). The trade study compares four configurations: baseline passive, active SMA continuous (fails endurance), clutch‑SMA + PCM only (rebound risk), and full AMPS v3.0. Only the full configuration exceeds the minimum utility threshold of 0.85 across all stakeholder groups.

